    "title": "'I just feel empty': Driver suspected in fatal hit-and-run in Brown County charged - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Chris Arnold, WKRC ,\n9 hours ago BROWN COUNTY, Ohio (WKRC) - The man believed to have been behind the wheel when a pedestrian was struck and killed in a hit-and-run in Brown County now faces charges. Michael Guillermin faces vehicular homicide, vehicular manslaughter, and failure to stop charges. The failure to stop charges are second-degree felonies that carry a sentence of two to eight years each if Guillermin is convicted. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 1",
